ed verification with diff-scoped test [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]selection[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Agents verify a change with a diff-scoped, gate-free `just check` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that costs ~1 core-minute instead of ~61 worker-minutes, `just [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]check-full` preserves today's exhaustive contract for landing and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]CI, and selection health (what was skipped, and whether skipping it[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]was ever wrong) is a measured, machine-readable metric rather than [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]an assumption.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]test_suite_tier1.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/test_suite_tier1.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-fp[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-fp/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Static import-graph selection engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine: build the cached import-graph selector, its depth-bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reverse closure, the broadening/escalation rules, and the JSON selection[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]manifest, plus the tools/select_tests CLI. No runner or Justfile [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Curated contract/audit test set[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: add the `contract` pytest marker, curate the repository-wide [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit tests behind it to a measured serial-runtime budget, generate a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]committed manifest from the marker, and add drift and budget guards.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scoped run mode and the no-lease path[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]runner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine, contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]runner: add a `scoped` mode to tools/run_pytest that runs the selection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serially with the suite-gate explicitly disabled, escalates to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]governed full lane when the selection is too large, and never queues for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tokens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]just check / just check-full split[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]check-split[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]check-split: repoint `just check` at the scoped lane, add `just [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check-full` carrying today's exhaustive behaviour, and update [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs/development.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and the CI guard tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Selection health metrics and false-negative detection[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]health[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health: persist selection manifests to a durable host-local store, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detect when a full run fails a test a recent scoped run excluded, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add `just selection-health` to summarize coverage, escalation, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]false-negative rates.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Coverage-context ground truth for selection[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contexts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine, health[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contexts: add --cov-context=test to the CI coverage leg, publish the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contexts database as an artifact, and teach the engine to prefer [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-test coverage ground truth over the static closure when a fresh [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline is available.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Two-speed verification policy in SASE memory[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]policy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after check-split, health[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]policy: obtain live user permission, then record the two-speed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verification contract in sase/memory and regenerate the derived [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction files.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-fp","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-fp.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-5b8da8337105d924d35dc926abd90270","started_at":"2026-08-06T00:57:48.442663+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785983451,"sha":"8c4e14ab0f564eee9242e66ac21f2d82d53f0027","subject":"feat(tests): add a scoped run mode to the pytest runner"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"de59910095bf6f69f9b4ec10e1ce909612d8dd779ee9a505426422039b8976fc","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-fp.3/chat.md","size_bytes":5936},"commits":{"digest":"0b8c2c2490f3ae74287ff47b69e53928d42c5ee6a88857778edd0f277c702599","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-fp.3/commits.json","size_bytes":233},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf